    {
      "entryId": "num-21-9",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Moses makes a bronze serpent and sets it on a pole; whoever is bitten and looks upon it lives. Jesus directly applies this to His own crucifixion: as Moses lifted up the serpent, so must the Son of Man be lifted up, that whoever believes in Him should not perish but have eternal life. First principle: God turns the emblem of the curse into the instrument of life when looked upon in faith.",
      "density": 3.825,
      "words": 73,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 35,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "num-21-8",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Make thee a fiery serpent, and set it upon a pole: and it shall come to pass, that every one that is bitten, when he looketh upon it, shall live. Remedy mirrors plague: what killed becomes the instrument of life when lifted up. First principle: salvation is by looking — faith fastened on the God-provided object.",
      "density": 3.1143,
      "words": 56,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 30,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "num-12-6",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The LORD declares the biblical criteria for the prophetic gift: \"If there be a prophet among you, I the LORD will make myself known unto him in a vision, and will speak unto him in a dream.\" Together with Isaiah 8:20 (harmony with the law) and Matthew 7:20 (\"by their fruits ye shall know them\"), Scripture establishes objective, empirical tests for true spiritual gifts. First principle: genuine prophetic manifestations operate under strict biblical boundaries, never overriding or contradicting the written canon.",
      "density": 2.9964,
      "words": 81,
      "sentences": 4,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "Matthew 7:20",
          "Isaiah 8:20"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "num-24-17",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Balaam, hired to curse Israel, can only bless: I shall see him, but not now... there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Israel. First principle: God turns every curse of the enemy into messianic blessing; the promised Ruler appears at God's appointed time, not nigh but certain.",
      "density": 2.7464,
      "words": 55,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "num-35-30",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "One witness cannot kill; two or more establish the matter. First principle: due process is divine law — the two-or-three witness rule Jesus and Paul both invoke for church and judgment alike.",
      "density": 2.0571,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
